# Deep Compliance Scan of All Four Manuscript Audits

**Scope:** current `revised_sustainability_manuscript.md`, checked against the two critical audits and the two architectural audits  
**Date:** 14 August 2026

## Executive finding

Most architectural findings from all four audits have been incorporated. The revised manuscript now has typed constraint semantics, prospectively frozen identity, two architecture-sensitive operators, explicit boundary interfaces, typed dependency hypergraphs, commons nodes, relation-level contract modalities, horizon typing, implementable-control language, nonstationary composition objects, and disciplined conjecture/placeholder labels.

However, **seven valid audit findings remain incompletely incorporated**, including one critical formal type error that survived the revision: the viability operator quantifies a policy \(\pi\) as if it were an element of the implementable action set \(U^{\mathrm{impl}}\). The architecture must distinguish action correspondences from causal policy classes. Articles 001 and 002 already contain the mathematical objects needed to repair this.

A further editorial issue remains: several sentences still read as revision history (“the earlier distinction,” “the previous manuscript,” “is replaced,” “is retired”). These should be removed from the scholarly manuscript.

