## 3. Remaining finding R2 — the two operators lack one official system-level assessment map

### Severity

**Major architectural clarification.**

### Current problem

The manuscript has a typed trajectory predicate, Operator I, Operator II, and an output portfolio. It does not define one official map connecting them into mutually exclusive system-level statuses.

### Required incorporation

Define an assessment map such as

\[
\mathfrak S_\Omega(z_0,q_0)
\in
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
\text{currently viable},\\
\text{recoverable within architecture},\\
\text{transformationally viable},\\
\text{infeasible within known architectures},\\
\text{indeterminate}
\end{array}
\right\},
\]

with typed subverdict \((P,F,N,R,E)\). “Recoverable within architecture” should use capture through an emergency envelope. “Transformationally viable” should require a hybrid path to a destination kernel. This would lock the relation among current viability, recovery, and transformation.

