## 6. Remaining finding R5 — novelty and relation to existing viable-sustainability work remain underdeveloped

### Severity

**Major publication-positioning task, not a defect in the architecture itself.**

### Current problem

The manuscript cites viability, resilience, SES, ecological economics, and safe-and-just-space traditions and includes a novelty test. It does not yet conduct the systematic comparison needed to support claims of an architectural advance.

### Required incorporation

Add a contribution matrix comparing at least:

- classical and robust viability theory;
- viable-sustainability and renewable-resource viability literature;
- epistemic/partial-observation viability;
- contract-based and compositional invariance;
- social–ecological systems and commons governance;
- strong sustainability and critical natural capital;
- safe-and-just-space frameworks;
- hybrid, sampled-data, RFDE, and information-state safety.

The novelty claim should identify which contribution is a new theorem, new synthesis, new interface, new counterexample, or new research programme. Articles 001 and 002 substantially strengthen this section but have not yet been merged into the master literature review.

